WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.670
In Japan, researchers put a ring
of cars on a circular track.

2
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:07.730
The drivers were asked
to do one simple thing:

3
00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:09.670
hold a steady speed.

4
00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.950
No obstacle, no crash.

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.310
Yet small speed changes built
up into a stop-start jam.

6
00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:19.110
So how could a computer
predict a jam like that,

7
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.970
before it even happens?

8
00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:25.590
In this mission, you'll see how any
computer system can be described as input,

9
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:27.570
process and output.

10
00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:30.910
You'll compare sequential
models, one step after another,

11
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:34.410
with parallel ones, where
parts run at the same time.

12
00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:38.790
And you'll find out how simulation
software lets you ask what if.

13
00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:43.520
Your mission: explain how a computer
can predict a jam with no crash.
